                <pb facs="0617" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg497"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.458 Haiti/13: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-09T17:00:00-04:00">July 9, 1931—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>49. The following message has been received by the President from the President
                    of Haiti: [Here follows text of telegram of July 4, printed on <ref
                        target="#pg491">page 491</ref>.]</p>
                <p>The President has replied as follows: [Here follows text of telegram of July 9,
                    printed <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>] Unless you perceive objection
                    thereto you may state to President Vincent that the President learns with
                    pleasure of his desire to contribute to an early settlement of the outstanding
                    problems between the two countries, and that he feels it a matter for mutual
                    satisfaction that the terms of the joint Haitianization program proposed by you
                    to the Haitian Government in accordance with the Department’s telegram No. 47 of
                    July 3 are not only in accord with the recommendations of the Forbes Commission
                    but envisage an even more speedy Haitianization of the Treaty Services.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
